|~ What is declared under `::call`, the step that calls a name: the
   refusals of a call, a name that names nothing, a value applied as a
   verb, a call too deep, a failure of a host's implementation. ~|

:call/PayloadNotSchemaError
  |~~ A `::call` is a map of `:name`, a keyword, and `:args`, a vector
      of quotes; `:field` names the field that does not fit, null when
      the payload is no map.
      ::link~(::call | doc)

      ~(
        ::call{:name 42}
        !| [type /field]
        |  eq [::call/PayloadNotSchemaError :name]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:call/ReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The `::call` prints as text that reads back as another step,
      or as none: `:printed` is that text.
      ::link~(::call | doc)

      ~(
        ::call{:name :"a b"}
        !| [type /printed]
        |  eq [::call/ReadBackDiffersError "a b"]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:call/HostFailureError
  |~~ A failure of the host's implementation: an error of the language
      the runtime is written in escaped a verb, which is a defect of
      that verb's host. `:name` carries the host's class name,
      `:message` its text, `:operand` the step that ran it and
      `:causes` the chain of host errors behind it, each with its own
      `:name` and `:message`. The step and the input are those of
      any error; recovery is a `!|` step, and the repair belongs to
      the host.
      ::link~(::call | doc)
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:call/ValueTakesNoModifiersError
  |~~ A name the scope binds to a value takes no modifiers.
      `:addresses` names where a verb of that name lives, one the
      declaration shadows among them, which a call by address reaches.
      ::link~(::call | doc)

      ~(
        5 | :five / | five 42
        !| [type /name /actualType]
        |  eq [::call/ValueTakesNoModifiersError :five ::number]
       )
      ~(:sort 5 | [3 1] | sort ~(/a) !| /addresses | has ::vec/sort)
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:call/EffectMarkMissingError
  |~~ A verb whose body calls a name marked `@` was called by a name
      without the mark. A declaration that names such a verb is refused
      where it stands, `::bind/EffectMarkMissingError`; this one is met
      when a host put the verb in the scope under a plain name, where no
      declaration was there to refuse it, and the host binds it under a
      name that carries the mark, `@fetch`.
      ::link~(::call | doc)
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:call/KindAnswersNoVerbError
  |~~ The kind of the subject has no verb of the name: `:actualType`
      names the kind, and `:addresses` the verbs of the name and the kinds
      they serve, so the subject is turned into one of those kinds first,
      or a verb of another name was meant. The call reached the contract
      of the name, a verb without a body, which answers no call.

      ~(1 | count !| [/actualType (/addresses | has ::vec/count)] | eq [::number true])

      ~(
        5 | count
        !| [type /addresses]
        |  eq [::call/KindAnswersNoVerbError #[::map/count ::set/count ::string/count ::vec/count]]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:call/UnknownNameError
  |~~ No name of the scope and no verb of the kinds of the subject
      answers the name. `:identifierName` holds the name as typed,
      `:addresses` where verbs of that name live under other kinds, and
      `:nearest` the names it was likely meant to be: those
      within an edit distance of a third of its length, one at least,
      and of those the nearest alone, in the order of their spelling.
      An edit is an insertion, a deletion, a substitution or a swap of
      two neighbours. A name with nothing near holds `[]`.
      ::link~(::call | doc)

      ~(
        thisIsNotDefined
        !| [type]
        |  eq [::call/UnknownNameError]
       )
      ~(fist !| /nearest | eq [:first])
      ~(
        :Box ::spec~() | :Ring ::spec~()
        | :Box/area ::verb~(1) | :Ring/area ::verb~(2)
        | 5 | area
        !| /addresses
        |  eq #[::Box/area ::Ring/area]
       )
      ~(:limit 3 | limti !| /nearest | eq [:limit])
      ~(zzzzqqq !| /nearest | eq [])
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:call/UnknownAddressError
  |~~ A name with a path names nothing: no declaration wrote that
      address. `:address` holds the address as a tag name, which the
      axes read, and `:nearest` the addresses it was likely meant to
      be. An address that names a value reads it, as a bare name does.
      ::link~(::call | doc)

      ~(
        [1 2 3] | vec/nothing
        !| [type /address]
        |  eq [::call/UnknownAddressError ::vec/nothing]
       )
      ~([1] | vec/countt !| /nearest | has ::vec/count)
      ~(:Box ::spec~() | :Box/side 3 | Box/side | eq 3)
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:call/EvaluationDepthExceededError
  |~~ A call too deep: every verb body, modifier, `apply` and
      constructor of a tag runs one frame below the step that called
      it, and the frame past the budget refuses, `:depth` the refused
      frame and `:limit` the budget. A verb that calls itself without a
      base case is refused here, on the fail track, while the host's
      memory stays bounded.
      ::link~(::call | doc)

      ~(
        :inf ::verb~(add 1 | inf) | 0 | inf
        !| type | eq ::call/EvaluationDepthExceededError
       )
      ~(
        :q ~(apply q) | apply q
        !| gt /depth /limit
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()
